  "geometryBasis": "Current named multipolygon, courtyard opening, main dome, courtyard fountain canopy and six mapped minaret bases. Original elevation tiles supply the hill profile and terrace contact.",
  "sectionBasis": "Diyanet and the Turkish Presidency report the completed 34 m diameter dome rising to 72 m and two groups of minarets, four of 107.1 m with three balconies and two of 90 m with two balconies. The exact 2024 Qualla photo gives a distant view of the standing cluster and its raised hilltop silhouette.",
  "limitations": [
    "The main 34 m roof and six 107.1 m or 90 m minarets use documented dimensions. Spacing and footprints follow the native map. Subordinate semi-domes, arcades, fenestration, terrace, colors, finish and ornamental detail are approximate.",
    "The original published Qualla view is distant. Exterior detail is derived from factual records and the mapped geometry. The below-terrace museum interior, underground garage, subway, detached visitor facilities and interior calligraphy are outside scope."
